ogic approach to ecogenetics. Am J Human Genet 42:89&#x02013;95 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3337114</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Khoury</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>James</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Population and family relative risks of disease associated with environmental factors in the presence of gene-environment interaction</article-title><source>Am J Epidemiol</source><year>1993</year><volume>137</volume><fpage>1241</fpage><lpage>1250</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Khoury MJ, James LM (1993) Population and family relative risks of disease associated with environmental factors in the presence of gene-environment interaction. Am J Epidemiol 137:1241&#x02013;1250 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8322764</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lasky-Su</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Faraone</surname><given-names>SV</given-names></name><name><surname>Lange</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsuang</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Doyle</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Smoller</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Laird</surname><given-names>NM</given-names></name><name><surname>Biedermand</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A study of how socioeconomic status moderates the relationship between SNPs encompassing BDNF and ADHD symptom count in ADHD families</article-title><source>Behav Genet</source><year>2007</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>487</fpage><lpage>497</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s10519-006-9136-x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Lasky-Su J, Faraone SV, La